  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-19T22:02:34.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-text-tags-684ed02c-6af3-4517-bca6-71121070fafd",
        "text": "Just like you organize notes in a binder, HTML uses special tags to structure text on a webpage.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d5f04284daf137a23d3f16957fd0cb02-test-lesson-intro-text-tags-panel-1-c0d1ef0a-7d07-4a5d-a2f5-9e4d2458ddce.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-text-tags-e9f58054-0f99-4644-bc23-2fed3bfb2fb0",
        "text": "Headings, like `<h1>` or `<h2>`, are like chapter titles or big section dividers. They tell readers what's most important!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/00468c2e43ff2d1c9c14c88b7cc52d2e-test-lesson-intro-text-tags-panel-2-3dd89abf-354b-4ab0-b97c-6cfc3bed2478.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-text-tags-9f5240d5-cba5-4b2e-a936-96a9e108d404",
        "text": "Paragraphs, using `<p>` tags, hold the main ideas and details. Think of them as the sentences and notes within each section.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5ea311aa0bb5bf6ff0a5a4ebe250711d-test-lesson-intro-text-tags-panel-3-4fec1261-bb85-4f33-baaf-ccae04108434.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-text-tags-644f4519-7e85-4780-a619-b302fa8f6b06",
        "text": "Lists, like `<ul>` (unordered) and `<ol>` (ordered) with `<li>` items, are perfect for organizing steps or groups of related ideas!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/be78de88067fc163a2c71ab0fa4f3709-test-lesson-intro-text-tags-panel-4-abeb0c03-8a7e-4e61-9cfc-6f4c50024854.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-text-tags-051640c4-b7b0-441a-911f-9be000f80817",
        "text": "Using headings, paragraphs, and lists makes your webpage super easy to read and understand, just like a well-organized binder!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/a0dae2e96005a0b286cd02abd5b43038-test-lesson-intro-text-tags-panel-5-b03284db-eaee-4bd3-9464-782c2d286511.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Introduce the concept of HTML tags used for structuring text content. Explain the purpose of headings, paragraphs, and lists in making web content readable and organized. Use a simple analogy or visual metaphor to illustrate content organization."
  },
